WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.080
I was lucky enough to actually host an HBO panel

2
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.950
where you and I in depthly spoke about

3
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.570
your process in "The Undoing."

4
00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.160
And I was wondering if you would tell us

5
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:16.730
about how you treated this character

6
00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:21.730
in defining the multi-facets of him.

7
00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:23.500
I do remember that I have felt

8
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.003
I was playing two characters.

9
00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.090
And that they were both real.

10
00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.980
Obviously the most real was guilty Jonathan,

11
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.050
who was a sociopath.

12
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:38.050
Narcissistic sociopath who only really loved himself.

13
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.680
And couldn't love anyone else,

14
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.240
couldn't feel for anyone else

15
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.390
and who is capable of killing

16
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:48.630
without feeling even a smidgen of remorse.

17
00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.910
But there was also innocent Jonathan,

18
00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.350
the Jonathan who presented himself to the world.

19
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:55.660
And he wasn't exactly a lie

20
00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:59.010
because Jonathan had convinced himself

21
00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.990
that that was really the real him.

22
00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.630
And that it was not even conceivable

23
00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.540
that this great doctor, this great healer of children,

24
00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:09.990
this wonderful father, this wonderful husband,

25
00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:13.170
this charming man about Manhattan

26
00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.520
could possibly be a killer.

27
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.930
So all those five and a half episodes

28
00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.517
I spend in that series saying,

29
00:01:20.517 --> 00:01:22.840
"I'm, I didn't kill her.

30
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.000
I didn't kill her.

31
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.290
I may have been a little unfaithful, but I didn't kill her.

32
00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:27.123
And I love you."

33
00:01:27.123 --> 00:01:28.540
He believes all that.

34
00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.890
And it was very important that he does believe it

35
00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.980
because, you know, all the evidence pointed to my guilt

36
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.550
and to preserve the whodunit aspect of that series,

37
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:41.910
I needed to be convincing when I was denying my guilt.

38
00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:42.821
I love it.

39
00:01:42.821 --> 00:01:46.730
And a true sociopathic narcissist, if you've studied them,

40
00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.830
that is the exact behavior.

41
00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:50.930
Yeah, they believe their lies.

42
00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.410
They create their own narrative

43
00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.950
and they're, and it's infallible.

44
00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:57.390
And the only thing that snowballs for them

45
00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:02.390
is further truth actually, upon the lies.

46
00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:06.399
So you can't even peel back the layers to get to the truth.

47
00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:09.730
You just get so far and it just happens to be

48
00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:13.120
a character trait I studied profusely

49
00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.137
and I was just so-

50
00:02:14.137 --> 00:02:16.911
Which boyfriend or husband was like that?

51
00:02:16.911 --> 00:02:18.550
(audience laughs)
(Drew coughs coyly)

52
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.930
I'll tell you where the cameras aren't rolling.

53
00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:23.240
But yeah, I'm, listen, I know.

54
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.790
And also, you know, there's a huge amount

55
00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:30.240
that goes in the political game of sociopathic narcissism.

56
00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.910
It falls into gas lighting.

57
00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.810
There's an extraordinary amount of behavior

58
00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.620
that occurs from one human being

59
00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.693
in a position of power,

60
00:02:39.693 --> 00:02:42.400
or a family member

61
00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.010
that does put on a charade that puts other people

62
00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:48.270
in a washing machine.

63
00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:50.297
And it's a very different.

64
00:02:50.297 --> 00:02:52.230
To me, the common denominator

65
00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.340
in all those people is narcissism.

66
00:02:55.340 --> 00:02:57.430
It's incredible self love.

67
00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.330
And you see it a lot in show business.

68
00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:03.210
But you see it a lot in politics.

69
00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.490
Which of course some people say

70
00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.098
is show business for the ugly.

71
00:03:06.098 --> 00:03:09.760
(audience claps and cheers)
(Drew laughs)

72
00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.640
I've never heard that one before,

73
00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.490
but I'll never forget it.

74
00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:16.653
Well, Hubert.

75
00:03:17.578 --> 00:03:22.540 line:15%
I just think my lucky stars that I get to know you

76
00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.300 line:15%
and that I still know you,

77
00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:29.050 line:15%
and I'm so happy for your family and your life,

78
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.420
and just everything that you've given to us.

79
00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.390
And I love that you're sassy and curmudgeony.

80
00:03:35.390 --> 00:03:39.570
And just send Hubert kisses off into the air.

81
00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.541
To you and your five beautiful children

82
00:03:41.541 --> 00:03:46.070
and your sexy mean, which you need probably,

83
00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:47.088
beautiful wife.

84
00:03:47.088 --> 00:03:48.145
(audience laughs)

85
00:03:48.145 --> 00:03:49.290
(Hugh chuckles)

86
00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:50.123
Yeah.

87
00:03:50.123 --> 00:03:52.950
Well, it's been lovely to see you Drew.

88
00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.760
I'll see you in the, what was it called?

89
00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.593
The Waverly Inn.

90
00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.463
But behave yourself.

91
00:03:58.463 --> 00:04:01.120
I'll meet you at the Waverly Inn, baby.

92
00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.630
HBO's original series "The Undoing"

93
00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.367
is streaming now on HBO max.

94
00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:09.450 line:15%
